{
  "name": "building-lifecycle",
  "description": "Building lifecycle: place, upgrade to T2, move, then demolish",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42 staffed:true",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42 staffed:true"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 50000,
          "buildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build management_office at:3,5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickIfPresent",
          "selector": "#bs-inspector [data-panel-close]",
          "timeoutMs": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"build\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"management_office\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 3,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "orderedBuildingCount": 1
        },
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -8000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "wait_until field:buildingCount equals:1 max_ticks:400",
      "description": "Let the queued construction site(s) be walked to and built out (#556): ordering a building no longer places it, so everything below that needs a standing building waits here first.",
      "timeout": 130,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitUntil",
          "field": "buildingCount",
          "equals": 1,
          "maxTicks": 400,
          "timeoutMs": 120000
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1,
          "orderedBuildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "build upgrade 1",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "ensurePanel",
          "panel": "build"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-building-id=\"1\"] .bs-build-row-name"
        },
        {
          "type": "awaitUsable",
          "selector": "#bs-inspector [data-action=\"upgrade\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-inspector [data-action=\"upgrade\"]"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Placed rows carry no Upgrade (#515, #1768): the player opens building #1's inspector and clicks its Upgrade action. A plain new_game site has no quests, so tier 2 is purchasable at once; the upgrade is ordered in place and the building stays counted.",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1
        },
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ]
      },
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "build list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "build move 2 to:10,5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build move 2 to:10,5"
        }
      ],
      "description": "role: bootstrap (issue #515): building #2 was never placed, so there is no row and no button in the DOM at all \u2014 not merely disabled. `expect.blocked` needs a present-but-unusable control (interaction-driver.ts's checkGoal refuses an absent selector: \"not in the DOM, so blocked proves nothing\"), which doesn't exist here, and no player can ever target an id that was never shown to them. Genuinely bootstrap: this exercises the console's own bad-id guard, not a control a player could reach either way.",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1
        },
        "note": "rejected: Building #2 not found \u2014 only building #1 was ever placed"
      },
      "role": "bootstrap",
      "commandOutcome": "refused"
    },
    {
      "command": "build list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "build destroy 2",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build destroy 2"
        }
      ],
      "description": "role: bootstrap (issue #515): same reasoning as the `build move 2` step above \u2014 building #2 was never placed, so there is no row and no button in the DOM to point `expect.blocked` at, and no player can ever target an id that was never shown to them.",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1
        },
        "note": "rejected: Building #2 not found \u2014 the real building #1 is still standing"
      },
      "role": "bootstrap",
      "commandOutcome": "refused"
    },
    {
      "command": "build list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    }
  ]
}
